      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u explain the difference between high glycemic index foods and low glycemic index foods? also why does it matter for insulin?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High glycemic index (GI) foods are quickly digested, causing a rapid spike in blood sugar levels, whereas low GI foods are digested slowly, causing a gradual increase in blood sugar. The GI index measures how the body responds to carbohydrates by breaking them down into glucose. Foods with a high GI (above 70) can lead to swings in blood sugar levels, insulin resistance, and increased insulin production, which matters because excessive insulin can lead to weight gain, insulin resistance, and a higher risk of chronic diseases like diabetes and heart disease.",
