      "content": "Besides diet, other lifestyle factors can contribute to blood sugar spikes. Stress and emotions, sleep deprivation, and physical activity patterns can all impact insulin sensitivity and blood sugar control. Additionally, certain medications and health conditions, such as polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS), Cushing's syndrome, and thyroid dysfunction, can also lead to blood sugar imbalances. Considering lifestyle adjustments, like incorporating stress-reducing activities, improving sleep habits, and increasing physical activity in the morning, may help regulate your blood sugar.",
